From: Maicon Alves <alvesmaiconn@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:49:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 04/13] formspec: fit fixed-size forms to screens under 800x600

size[w,h,true] locks a form to a base screen of 800x600: it is laid
out and centered as if the screen were that big, shifted by half the
extra space when the real screen is bigger, and not at all when it is
smaller. On a 640x480 screen such a form (the main menu's "create
world" dialog, for one) is centered at (400,300) instead of (320,240):
80 pixels right and 60 down, with its buttons off the screen.

Only lock when the screen is at least 800x600; below that the form is
sized to fit the screen and centered on it, as a form without the
fixed flag is (and as touch_gui already makes them all).

Upstream: not sent yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/gui/guiFormSpecMenu.cpp b/src/gui/guiFormSpecMenu.cpp
index 04a2a7089..6064f294c 100644
--- a/src/gui/guiFormSpecMenu.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/guiFormSpecMenu.cpp
@@ -337,7 +337,10 @@ void GUIFormSpecMenu::parseSize(parserData* data, const std::string &element)
 
 		lockSize(false);
 		if (!g_settings->getBool("touch_gui") && parts.size() == 3) {
-			if (parts[2] == "true") {
+			// on a screen smaller than the 800x600 base the form would be centered off it:
+			// fit it to the screen instead
+			const v2u32 screen = RenderingEngine::get_video_driver()->getScreenSize();
+			if (parts[2] == "true" && screen.X >= 800 && screen.Y >= 600) {
 				lockSize(true,v2u32(800,600));
 			}
 		}
